WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:08.230
It all began when some country launched
a genetically engineered bioweapon.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.740
This was swiftly responded to by the launch
of several retaliatory thermonuclear warheads.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.620
The war dragged on for years,

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.040
claiming countless lives from all over the globe.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.710
The few remaining survivors have
little interest in things like stars.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.710
Basically, what I'm trying to tell you is...

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.470
The society you remember is a thing of the past.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.850
I have attempted to query
the support center's databases,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.220
but I have been unable to connect.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.600
Not surprising.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.850
On a different note, Mr. Customer,

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:49.150
I think perhaps you may require this tool soon.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:50.360
Nope.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.230
Is that so?

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.990
I'm asking nicely now, stop sticking
your nose in every little thing.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.530
Order acknowledged.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.040
By the way, Mr. Customer,

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.710
will you be requiring the
assistance of this tool soon?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.380
Sure, help me out and
clamp your own mouth shut.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:23.640
<i>I don't even know why I'm doing this.</i>

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.810
<i>What I do know is that,
now that the sun has set,</i>

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.520
<i>venturing out is dangerous.</i>

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:35.150
<i>Also, this primitive contraption
is a lot hardier than it looks.</i>

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:41.870
Mr. Customer, how long do you estimate it will take
for your repairs on Miss Jena to be complete?

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:43.910
Hell if I know. Ain't got a clue.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:48.120
Will it be fixed in time for
tomorrow's 11:00 am projection?

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.920
I highly doubt it.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.920
If that is the case, may I put out a notice that
tomorrow's projections will be postponed?

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.510
Do whatever you want.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:59.800
Acknowledged. I will register
this as a critical directive.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.100
This light bulb's filament is burned out.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.020
Is there a spare—

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.270
Mr. Customer.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.860
I apologize for the inconvenience,
but it is almost midnight.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.900
As per protocol,
I will be switching into sleep mode.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:16.780
Huh?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.910
Reboot from sleep mode is scheduled for 9:00 am.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:24.620
Remaining operation time
after reboot will be 75 hours.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.910
Well then, good night.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.710
Hey, wait...

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:34.710
God damn it.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.860
Mr. Customer.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:05.280
Good morning, Mr. Customer.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.910
Were you the one calling me?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:07.620
Yes, sir.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.620
I was dreaming.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.380
Oh, how wonderful! Was it pleasant?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.880
Not at all...

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:20.760
As I am a robot, I am incapable of dreaming.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.550
But how shall I put it?

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.930
I have very much longed to experience it!

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.390
Most dreams are not worth longing after.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:31.390
Is that so?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.400
Wait a sec.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.860
So you're saying you're only operational
for one week out of the entire year?

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:39.740
Yes.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.990
For the past 30 years,

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:45.410
the quantity of electricity delivered to
this department store has declined sharply.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:49.370
Per protocol, I have activated energy-saving mode.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:55.880
Two days ago at 9:00 am, I became operational
for the first time in 8,601 hours.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:01.130
Just as I happened to be passing through.
Talk about bad timing...

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:06.430
Five days from now, at midnight,
I will return to recharging hibernation mode.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.890
I see.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.310
<i>To think, the emergency power's
still running after all that's happened...</i>

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:17.650
By the way, Mr. Customer, what do you
intend to do with that rainwater?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.740
Drink it.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:28.580
Unlike you, I'll die if I don't drink water.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:33.250
If you would like, I could prepare a beverage for you.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.120
A beverage?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.250
Yes.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:39.130
To tell you the truth,
brewing tea is one of my specialties.

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:41.630
Or perhaps you'd prefer
a freshly ground coffee?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.630
Coffee, huh...

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.260
How about alcohol, then?

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.470
I'm talking bottled distilled
liquor with unbroken seals.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.890
It's actually very important to me.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.180
Certainly, we have those in stock.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.890
Really?! Where?!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:05:00.150
Our department store has several vendors
located on B1 that sell high-grade liquor...

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:02.900
Yeah, yeah, I get the idea.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:03.740
Of course.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:10.740
In that case, Mr. Customer, may I inquire
about Miss Jena and her current state of repairs?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.250
No change from last night.
Repairs are still underway.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.000
I see...

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:23.090
In that case, I will go and announce
the cancellation of today's projection.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:29.720
Hey, do you have spare light bulbs
stored away somewhere?

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.680
Recently, two of the latest 905 series

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:39.190
have been assigned to the
help desk at the main entrance.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:44.190
Being FT models, they both have a much
more adult appearance compared to myself.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.820
Their faceplates are quite detailed,
and they even feature the capability to shed tears.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.830
Tears, huh. Try turning it on.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.410
Understood.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.710
This one's okay...

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:03.130
So what, you can't shed tears?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:04.130
Correct.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.760
Tear-generation functionality

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.090
was first introduced in the
predecessor models, the 9000 series.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.680
I see. Good for them.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.520
Switch on.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:17.310
Understood.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.560
This one's busted.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.860
Guess I have two usable ones...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.820
By the way, may I remove this cable now?

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:32.240
This is a shameful emergency measure
that I should not be showing to customers...

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:36.120
Wait a bit longer. I wanna try the motors.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.910
Understood.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:39.460
By the way, Mr. Customer.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:40.880
What is it now?

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.630
How does shedding tears feel?

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.550
Can't really say.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.510
When I'm crying,
I'm usually not thinking very clearly.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.890
Is that so?

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.430
I do not know how to put this,

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:58.480
but I would very much like to be able to shed tears.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:02.520
As I am an Economy Edition model,
I lack that functionality.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.820
Let's just say you're not really
missing out on anything.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.110
Is that so?

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.150
Yeah, no doubt about it.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.030
All righty.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.450
Move the latitude axis upwards, bit by bit.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.280
Yes, sir.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:20.540
For your safety, please evacuate from the radius of revolution.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:49.820
Mr. Customer, might you have an estimated
time of completion for the repairs of Miss Jena?

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:50.950
Who knows?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:55.240
Do you think it will be in time
for tomorrow's 11:00 am projection?

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.830
Dunno. Feel free to pray to God.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:03.620
Which god should I pray to, then?

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.580
What'd you say?

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.960
For instance, there are the ancient Greek gods:

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:15.430
Zeus, Athena, Apollo, Hermes,
Artemis, Demeter, Poseidon, Hades...

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.100
You sure know a lot.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.350
Just pick your favorite or whatever.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:23.230
Understood. In that case, I shall pray to Dionysus.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.100
Who the hell is that?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:29.360
The god of wine and fertility,
also known by his Roman name, Bacchus.

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:32.610
I felt that this god would surely
be most to your liking, Mr. Customer.

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:35.740
Well, you're not too far off...

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:39.120
Pray to your god, not mine.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:41.290
My god?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.870
The god of robots.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:50.130
The information you have requested
does not match any entry in my database.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.800
I see.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.720
However, I have found something related.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.090
This is from a meeting we had

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.850
about the mythological heavens,
which we featured as a special presentation.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.100
I have the file saved as a hologram.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.270
Is there a heaven for robots?

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:10.820
Hm?

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:13.650
Of course there is! There has to be!

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:14.570
Right, manager?

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.780
Ah, yes, that's right.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:19.030
What is that place like?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.700
Well...

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:25.790
It's free of malfunctions and
batteries never decay! Right?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:31.840
Huh? Um, yeah, and no software bugs
or any need to replace parts, I heard.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:35.510
You'll be granted all your other wishes too!

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:36.970
Is that so?

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.550
Yes, yes.

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.850
I see.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.810
The god you're looking for is the one
in that robot heaven. Keep that in mind.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.860
Understood. Critical data registered.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.280
I am very pleased to have learned about this god.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:01.240
In fact, I have a wish I would like
to ask the God of Robots to grant.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:02.330
A wish?

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.750
What could you possibly want?

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.330
Well, it is about Heaven...

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.630
What is it?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.750
Mr. Customer.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:18.590
I apologize for the inconvenience,
but it is almost midnight.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:23.930
As per protocol,
I will be switching into sleep mode.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.770
It's gotten that late already?

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:30.400
Reboot from sleep mode is scheduled for 9:00 am.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.780
Remaining operation time
after reboot will be 60 hours.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.190
Well then, good night.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.420
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:57.300
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:10:59.260
All the stars in the sky await...

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.300
Hey, I'm done.

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:07.810
Mr. Customer, are you saying that you
have completed your repairs on Miss Jena?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.810
Yeah, that's right.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.980
I've done all I can.
